# Community Mental Health Services and Daily Living Skills: The Relevance of a Home Economics Curriculum.

**Authors:** Cunningham, Flora E., Weis, David L.

## Abstract
Community treatment settings offer home economists an opportunity to participate actively in the deinstitutionalization of mental health clients. Behavioral objectives for these clients are examined in the following areas: personal health and safety, community awareness, housing, nutrition, clothing and personal appearance, and financial management. (CT)

